            <ArticleTitle>[Spontaneous uterine rupture due to uterine leiomyosarcoma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>86</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11604/pamj.2016.24.86.8849</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Uterine sarcomas are rare cancers characterized by clinical and histological polymorphism. They are malignant tumors of poor prognosis. Inaugural manifestation of acute abdomen with hemo-pneumoperitoneum and spontaneous uterine rupture remains exceptional. The authors report the case of a uterine leiomyosarcoma manifesting itself as an inaugural generalized acute peritonitis in a 43 year old woman. Uterine rupture due to malignant tumor was suspected during urgent preoperative imaging (ultrasound and CT scan) and confirmed histologically.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
